{
  "_comment": "1.21.1 neoforge mod-compat batch 07 of 13: Industrial Upgrade, Integrated Dynamics, Integrated Terminals, Iskandert's Utilities, JEI, JourneyMap, Keyboard Wizard CE, Keymap Since 0.8.0-beta.1. Same harness row as envs/1.21.1-neoforge.json (uitest/1.21.1-neoforge), so this file adds no Gradle row; the mods below are tagged \"harness\", so jt hands their pinned jars to that row as -PjechExtraJars and it loads them exactly as it loads jech/jei — every jar dev-classpath, because a standalone row stages nothing. Targets are authored as newest-release (describe.version \"\") and pinned by jt resolve. integratedcrafting and refined-storage are here because NeoForge force-loads every @GameTestHolder class at startup and the Cyclops 1.11.1/1.38.1 gametest classes link org.cyclops.integratedcrafting.* (Integrated Terminals) and com.refinedmods.refinedstorage.* (Integrated Dynamics' integrateddynamicscompat) while declaring those mods nowhere in their metadata.",
